Debounce delays execution until calls stop for a set period; throttle runs at most once per fixed interval regardless of call frequency.

- Debounce: resets the timer on every call. Use for search-input, resize-end, autosave.
- Throttle: fires on a fixed cadence, ignoring extra calls in between. Use for scroll handlers, mousemove, rate-limited API calls.
- Debounce can delay indefinitely if calls keep coming; throttle guarantees periodic execution.

```js
function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), wait);
  };
}

function throttle(fn, wait) {
  let last = 0;
  return (...args) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now - last >= wait) {
      last = now;
      fn(...args);
    }
  };
}
```

